  "step_3": "The decision reason requires (1) computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (4000, 3000, 0), and (2) comparing each lottery based on the probability that outcomes exceed this level. However, the individual does not mention or imply any calculation of an average outcome, nor any comparison of outcomes to a reference point. The individual only refers to the 25% chance of winning 3000 Euros as 'plausible', which may reflect a subjective judgment of adequacy but does not align with the structured rule of the aspiration-level reason. There is no evidence that the individual considered the 4000 Euro outcome in relation to a threshold, nor that they evaluated probabilities of exceeding such a threshold across lotteries. While the individual ends up focusing on Lottery B—same as the aspiration-level reason—the justification is qualitatively different. The match in choice does not imply use of the same reason. The verbal report lacks any indication of the key components of the decision reason (aspiration level, comparison of outcomes to it, probability of exceeding it).",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
